{title: 265 - Breathe on Me, Breath of God}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #265 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 265}
{meta: category Holy Spirit - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]Breathe on me, breath of God,
[Gb]Fill [Ab7/C]mewith [Ebm]life [Ab]anew,
[Ab]That I [Ab7]may love what [Bbm]Thou [Db/Ab]dostlove,
[Gb]Anddo [Fm/Ab]what [Ab7]Thou wouldst [Db]do.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]Breathe on me, breath of God,
[Gb]Until [Db]my [Ebm]heart [Ab]is pure,
[Ab]Until [Ab7]with Thee I [Bbm]will [Db/Ab]one [Gb]will,
[Gb]To do [Fm/Ab]and [Ab7]to endure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]Breathe on me, breath of God,
[Gb]Till [Ab7/C]I [Db]am [Ebm]wholly [Ab]Thine,
[Ab]Until [Ab7]this earthly [Bbm]part [Db/Ab]of [Gb]me
[Gb]Glows with [Fm/Ab]Thy [Ab7]fire divine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db]Breathe on me, breath of God,
[Gb]So [Ab7/C]shall [Db]I [Ebm]constant [Ab]be,
[Ab]And live [Ab7]with Thee the [Bbm]perfect [Gb]life
[Gb]Of Thine [Fm/Ab]eternity.
{end_of_verse}
